{"id":"649b44626bd5cc6f","group":"27","path":"27/27-df-selfdual.md","title":"Self-dual Boolean function","display":"df-selfdual — Self-dual Boolean function","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-df-selfdual","aliases":["27-df-selfdual"],"display":"df-selfdual — Self-dual Boolean function","depends_on":["[[27-df-dual]]"],"local_review_status":"2026-10-20-formalization-reviewed-source-text-not-rechecked"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-df-selfdual"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-df-selfdual</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-selfdual — Self-dual Boolean function"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b491e41297256b44\" href=\"?note=b491e41297256b44\" title=\"27-df-dual\">27-df-dual</a></span></div>"},{"key":"local_review_status","html":"2026-10-20-formalization-reviewed-source-text-not-rechecked"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Dual}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{Dual}_n\\)</span> (duality operator, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"b491e41297256b44\" href=\"?note=b491e41297256b44\" title=\"27-df-dual\">27-df-dual</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SelfDual}_n\\subseteq\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{SelfDual}_n\\subseteq\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SelfDual}_n\\coloneqq\\{f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\mid\\mathrm{Dual}_n(f)=f\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{SelfDual}_n\\coloneqq\\{f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\mid\\mathrm{Dual}_n(f)=f\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Equivalently, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f(x)=1-f(1-x)\">\\(f(x)=1-f(1-x)\\)</span> for every <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\\in\\mathbb{B}^{n}\">\\(x\\in\\mathbb{B}^{n}\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-dual","status":"resolved","id":"b491e41297256b44","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-dual]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-dual","status":"resolved","id":"b491e41297256b44","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Dual}_n$ (duality operator, see [[27-df-dual]])","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\mathbb N","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Dual}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SelfDual}_n\\subseteq\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SelfDual}_n\\coloneqq\\{f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\mid\\mathrm{Dual}_n(f)=f\\}","display":true},{"tex":"f(x)=1-f(1-x)","display":false},{"tex":"x\\in\\mathbb{B}^{n}","display":false}],"bytes":703,"backlinks":[{"id":"5244dbb38da17b8a","anchor":"ref-332","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[27-df-selfdual|df-selfdual — Self-dual Boolean function]]"},{"id":"d2ed815720a23b5c","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge1}$，$\\mathrm{SD}_n$ 见 [[27-df-selfdualextension]]，$\\mathrm{SelfDual}_{n+1}$ 见 [[27-df-selfdual]]。$B_n,B_{n+1}$ 与逆向限制映射 $R_0$ 由下式构造。"}],"outgoing":["b491e41297256b44"]}